# Check every text file out with LF, whatever the machine's core.autocrlf says.
# Several tests compare committed files byte-for-byte with what a generator
# produces (test-data/README.md, docs/EDGE_CASES.md), and Prettier expects LF,
# so a Windows checkout that rewrote them to CRLF failed on a clean clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The synthetic CSV is RFC 4180, which uses CRLF, and the generator writes it
# that way on purpose (server/prisma/test-data-files.ts). Stored and checked out
# byte-for-byte, with no conversion either way.
*.csv -text

*.pdf binary
*.png binary
